course: dictionary
lesson: 13402
title: Plant-eating animals
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Herbivorous is a science word. It means eating only plants, such as grass, leaves, fruit and seeds.
explain: Break it into parts: herb means a plant, and vorous means eating. So a herbivorous animal is a plant-eater. «The rabbit was herbivorous, nibbling clover in the field.» Clover is a plant, so the clues show what the word means.
explain: Science has three food words to compare. Carnivorous animals eat meat, herbivorous animals eat plants, and omnivorous animals eat both. Check which one fits by asking what the animal eats.
fact: Herbivorous means eating only plants.
fact: «Herbivorous» comes from herb (a plant) and -vorous (eating).
fact: Cows, rabbits, elephants and koalas are herbivorous.
fact: Many dinosaurs, such as «Triceratops», were herbivorous.
fact: In a food chain, herbivores are primary consumers, because they eat plants, and carnivores eat the herbivores.
exercise: What does «herbivorous» mean? | *Eating only plants | Living mostly in water | Eating both plants and meat | Eating only meat
exercise: Which of these animals is herbivorous? | Shark | *Koala | Hawk | Lion
exercise: Which word means eating both plants and meat? | carnivorous | ancient | herbivorous | *omnivorous
test: «The elephants in the herd were herbivorous, eating leaves and bark all day.» What did the elephants eat? | Insects only | Other animals | *Leaves and bark | Fish from the river
test: In a food chain, grass is eaten by a rabbit. What is the rabbit? | A producer that makes its own food | *A herbivore, a primary consumer | A carnivore, a meat-eater | A decomposer
exam: Which word describes an animal that eats only plants, like a «Triceratops»? | omnivorous | carnivorous | nocturnal | *herbivorous
